From ada5d8842ad5bee05c7a0da4defa21e29598be52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 01:54:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(render): reproduce the native Bedrock classic lightmap

Java 26.3 applies a different gamma transform and derives Nether ambient
light after its brightness curve. Render actual Bedrock Overworld and
Nether connections with a dedicated reloadable lightmap pipeline instead.
Keep immutable inputs in the render state, update when inputs change,
and close the native uniform buffer with its owning Java lightmap.

Port the scalar image builder and verified producers from the official
Bedrock 1.26.51.1 executable (SHA-256
537c0aee2e79afbdc94b44b28e00f466ae62bc50e2733d953b430db9dbaa9ee7):
146619c50 supplies block RGB, per-channel quartic gamma and byte truncation;
142313be0 supplies the native 16-float table with Nether's clamped +0.1;
1423122e0, 14230e620 and 146235f20 supply daylight, weather and sunrise;
14692cd30 supplies Nether's white sky and fixed full sky factor;
1448018f0 fixes both ambient bias stages on and the white boost off.
The ordinary contribution fixes the previous boss value to zero, so its
boss RGB branch stays absent instead of importing Java boss behavior.

Use the direct native-compatible gamma range and the native NV/conduit
duration curve. Darkness consumes Java's effect blend lifecycle, whose
exact native fade timing remains unverified. The End retains Java's
pipeline until its animated native sky input is established. Enhanced
lighting and resource-pack lighting overrides are outside this port.

Validate eight targeted input/uniform tests and the actual fragment shader
through Mesa EGL against an independent native float32 oracle. All 11,520
pixels across 45 scenarios match the reference bytes exactly.
